3938	4133	3706	3706	Oxenham	766	“ my merry men all , make up your minds what mannered men you be minded to be before you take your bounties . I want none of your rascally lurching longshore vermin , who get five pounds out of this captain , and ten out of that , and let him sail without them after all , while they are stowed away under women 's mufflers , and in tavern cellars . If any man is of that humor , he had better to cut himself up , and salt himself down in a barrel for pork , before he meets me again ; for by this light , let me catch him , be it seven years hence , and if I do not cut his throat upon the streets , it 's a pity ! But if any man will be true brother to me , true brother to him I 'll be , come wreck or prize , storm or calm , salt water or fresh , victuals or none , share and fare alike ; and here 's my hand upon it , for every man and all ! and so--
