83710	83896	83617	83617	he	1153	“ Tale of a Christian , sir . There was two boys pig - minding , seed him at it down the hill , beside a maiden that was taken mazed ( and no wonder , poor soul ! ) and lying in screeching asterisks now down to the mill -- you ask as you go by -- and saw the flames come out of the mouth of mun , and the smoke out of mun 's nose like a vire - drake , and the roaring of mun like the roaring of ten thousand bulls . Oh , sir ! and to go with he after dark over moor ! ' Tis the devil 's devices , sir , against you , because you'm going against his sarvants the Pope of Room and the Spaniard ; and you 'll be Pixy - led , sure as life , and locked into a bog , you will , and see mun vanish away to fire and brimstone , like a jack - o'-lantern . Oh , have a care , then , have a care ! ”
84036	84055	84057	84057	Yeo	769	“ Meat and drink ? Fall to , then , man , and do n't stand on manners . ”
