137974	138167	137931	137931	she	4841	“ Ah , Mr. Gilbert ! since first he went to Guinea after those poor negroes , little lightness has my heart known ; and the very day that that crest was put up in our grand new house , as the parson read the first lesson , there was this text in it , Mr. Gilbert , ' Woe to him that buildeth his house by iniquity , and his chambers by wrong . Shalt thou live because thou closest thyself in cedar ? ' And it went into my ears like fire , Mr. Gilbert , and into my heart like lead ; and when the parson went on , ' Did not thy father eat and drink , and do judgment and justice ? Then it was well with him , ' I thought of good old Captain Will ; and -- I tell you , Mr. Gilbert , those negroes are on my soul from morning until night ! We are all mighty grand now , and money comes in fast , but the Lord will require the blood of them at our hands yet , He will ! ”
